# Local development secrets — NEVER commit real values.
# Generate new secrets before production deployment and store via `wrangler secret put`.
#
# Required Environment Variables:
# ---------------------------------
# STAMP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY: AES-256-GCM key for encrypting credentials at rest
#   Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# STAGING_PERURI_USERNAME: Peruri staging API username
# STAGING_PERURI_PASSWORD: Peruri staging API password
#
# Production Secrets (set via wrangler secret put):
# ---------------------------------
# PERURI_PRODUCTION_USERNAME: Peruri production API username
# PERURI_PRODUCTION_PASSWORD: Peruri production API password
# PRODUCTION_TENANT_CREDENTIALS: Encrypted production credentials (if needed)

# Example values for local development only
STAMP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_GENERATED_KEY
STAGING_PERURI_USERNAME=staging@example.local
STAGING_PERURI_PASSWORD=staging-demo-password

# Optional: For production testing (set via wrangler secret put)
# PERURI_PRODUCTION_USERNAME=
# PERURI_PRODUCTION_PASSWORD=
